# Copy to .env for local development. Never commit the real .env.
#
# The app runs with none of these set. Everything below either has a sensible
# default or degrades gracefully, so `npm run dev` works on a fresh clone.

# --- Site -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Staging must set these, otherwise it advertises the production URL as its own
# canonical and asks search engines to index a duplicate of the live site.
# NUXT_SITE_URL=https://staging.garibaldipharmacy.com
# NUXT_SITE_INDEXABLE=false

# --- Server -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Bind to loopback in production so Caddy is the only way in.
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=3000
# Surfaced by /api/health so a deploy can prove which release is live.
# RELEASE_ID=

# --- Storage ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Lives outside the release directory so a rollback changes code, never data.
# DATA_DIR=/srv/garibaldi-prod/shared/data
# DATABASE_PATH=${DATA_DIR}/submissions.db
# UPLOADS_DIR=${DATA_DIR}/uploads
# UPLOAD_KEY_PATH=${DATA_DIR}/keys/uploads.key
#
# WARNING: back up UPLOAD_KEY_PATH separately from the data. Without the key the
# encrypted prescription images and insurance cards are unrecoverable noise.

# --- Spam -------------------------------------------------------------------
# With no site key the widget does not render; with no secret the server skips
# verification. Both must be set in production.
# NUXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
# Submissions allowed per IP per 10 minutes.
# SUBMIT_RATE_LIMIT=5

# --- Submissions view (/admin) ----------------------------------------------
# Fails CLOSED: with no hash set, /admin returns 503 and shows nothing.
# Generate both values with: node scripts/hash-admin-password.mjs
# ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=
# ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Dashboard sync (/api/sync) ---------------------------------------------
# Sealed-box export to shift-dashboard inside the pharmacy.
#
# Generate both values on the PHARMACY's server with the dashboard's key setup
# (shift-dashboard docs/deployment-guide.md, step 7). It prints exactly these
# two lines. scripts/generate-sync-keypair.mjs here is a fallback with the same
# formats.
#
# SYNC_PUBLIC_KEY is the public half only. This server seals prescription
# requests with it and can never open them again. The private key lives only on
# the pharmacy PC. Never put it here; doing so defeats the entire design.
#
# Both must be set or the sync endpoints return 503 and nothing is exported.
# SYNC_PUBLIC_KEY=
# SYNC_TOKEN_HASH=

# --- Email ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Resend over HTTPS, not SMTP: DigitalOcean blocks outbound 25, 465 and 587.
# With no API key, messages are logged instead of sent.
#
# One email per request: the patient's receipt (server/utils/receiptEmail.ts).
# Staff are not emailed; requests reach them through the dashboard. The
# receipt is no-reply: no Reply-To, and it asks patients to phone instead.
#
# Send from a dedicated subdomain. Do NOT verify the apex domain and do NOT edit
# the apex SPF record, which currently authorises Microsoft 365 for the
# pharmacy's real mail.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# MAIL_FROM=Garibaldi Pharmacy - No Reply <noreply@send.garibaldipharmacy.com>
